// THE CANONICAL SPELLING OF THIS HELPER IS ALREADY MATCHED IN THE REPO, AND IT
// IS NOT RETAIL'S SPELLING HERE.  game/GameEngine/Source/Common/
// Rva0005DC70CompareWideLengths.cpp is a byte-matched body of the same wide
// compare at 0x0005DC70 (77B, ledger row 17932, `matched`).  Retail 0x0005DC70
// emits the FOLDED shape at both exits (`sub eax,ecx; jne` for the diff and
// `mov eax,edi; sub eax,ebx` for the tail), and its source ends in a bare
// `return len1 - len2;`.  Retail 0x0062CCE0 inlines the same algorithm with
// BOTH exits redundant.  So the two bodies provably compiled from differently
// spelled sources, and this stash's `tail` local is the 0x62CCE0 spelling.
// Two consequences worth keeping:
//  - the helper is inlined three levels deep in 0x62CCE0 (compare(const
//    StringBase&) -> compare(const T*,int) -> the run compare), reading both
//    m_data headers, both lengths and both data pointers inline, with
//    g_bfmeEmptyUnicode as the null-data literal.  Any rewrite must keep all
//    three levels inlined or the 0x0115..0x0152 block changes.
