//   byte-identical to this shape: `unsigned int u` + `(int)u` copy; a second
//   named copy `const int d`; assignment inside the condition; the
//   `unsigned short` subtraction; a bare `return *p - *q` (drops to 547B/163);
//   a dead-code statement after the break; `(unsigned int)*p != (unsigned
//   int)*q` in the loop test; and q-before-p (which is 113, i.e. worse).  With
//   the three previously banked spellings, cluster B has had 11 and none
//   restores retail's `sub eax,edx; cmp eax,ebp; jne`.  MSVC reuses the sub's
//   flags because the block is only entered when `*p != *q`, and no source
//   spelling in the family breaks that.  Same verdict as R2: compiler-internal.
// The mechanical generators add nothing here either: tools/eh_levers.py
//   returns only per-callee `throw()` and `/EHsc-` (3 trials, no improvement)
//   and tools/shape_family_levers.py over sib,register,bool,test,copy,store,
//   loop,branch,constant,frame returns only two `frame` rewrites of the
//   compare helper's locals (3 trials, no improvement) -- neither generates a
//   store-order or loop-bound alternative for this body.
//
// NEXT LEVER IS NOT ANOTHER SPELLING.  It would have to change the register
// allocation itself, e.g. make the inner loop need a fifth callee-saved
// register so MSVC spills the node instead of taking ebp, or reach the body
